<LegalPage title="About ASCII Banner" description="A fast, private FIGlet browser built for developers who want to compare first and copy once.">
  <h2>Why this tool exists</h2>
  <p>Most ASCII banner generators ask you to select a font before you can see it. ASCII Banner reverses that workflow: type once, scan every style, and copy the result that fits your project.</p>
  <p>The generator is designed for practical developer output. It measures terminal columns and wraps the result for Markdown, source comments, shell scripts, or plain-text files.</p>
  <h2>Private by design</h2>
  <p>Rendering happens entirely in your browser. There is no account, database, upload endpoint, or server-side banner history. Favorites and up to 10 recent text entries stay on the current device and can be deleted locally.</p>
  <h2>Built on FIGlet</h2>
  <p>The rendering engine is powered by the open-source <a href="https://github.com/patorjk/figlet.js">figlet.js project</a>. Individual font attribution is shown on each font page and retained inside the distributed font file.</p>
  <h2>Editorial approach</h2>
  <p>We publish focused guidance for the most useful fonts and real developer workflows. The aim is not to create thousands of thin pages; it is to make each indexed page answer a specific question well.</p>
</LegalPage>
